  "slug": "mephit-mini-con",
  "name": "Mephit Mini Con",
  "shortName": "MMC",
  "description": "Mephit Mini Con (MMC) is a German-language furry convention held each spring in Europe, controlled by FurCon e.V. and chiefly organized by Pegasus. The first, in 1998, was a gathering of around twenty furs at an apartment in Rüsselsheim, Hesse, over the May Day weekend. It then moved through Seeheim and the Lorelei Rock area before settling in 2006 at Freusburg Castle in Kirchen, Rhineland-Palatinate, near Siegen, where Eurofurence 7 had also been held. Each year has a theme, and attendance has grown from twenty to about 200.",
